   {
    "field": "special",
    "value": "stored triglycerides (fat)",
    "quote": "Adipose tissue is made up of cells called adipocytes that collect and store fat in the form of triglycerides, for energy metabolism.",
    "source": {
     "section": "33.2 Animal Primary Tissues",
     "url": "https://openstax.org/books/biology-2e/pages/33-2-animal-primary-tissues",
     "license": "CC BY 4.0",
     "citation": "Clark MA, Douglas M, Choi J (2018). Biology 2e. OpenStax.",
     "access": "Access for free at https://openstax.org/books/biology-2e/pages/1-introduction"
    }
   },
   {
    "field": "function",
    "value": "Adipocytes are specialized fat stores: fat globules take up most of each cell's volume.",
    "quote": "Mammals store fats in specialized cells, or adipocytes, where fat globules occupy most of the cell’s volume.",
    "source": {
     "section": "3.3 Lipids",
     "url": "https://openstax.org/books/biology-2e/pages/3-3-lipids",
     "license": "CC BY 4.0",
     "citation": "Clark MA, Douglas M, Choi J (2018). Biology 2e. OpenStax.",
     "access": "Access for free at https://openstax.org/books/biology-2e/pages/1-introduction"
    }
   },
   {
    "field": "function",
    "value": "By holding the body's surplus energy as fat, adipocytes act as an energy reserve and also help insulate the body.",
    "quote": "Adipose cells store surplus energy in the form of fat and contribute to the thermal insulation of the body.",
    "source": {
     "section": "4.3 Connective Tissue Supports and Protects",
     "url": "https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/4-3-connective-tissue-supports-and-protects",
     "license": "CC BY 4.0",
     "citation": "Betts JG, Young KA, Wise JA, Johnson E, Poe B, Kruse DH, Korol O, Johnson JE, Womble M, DeSaix P (2022). Anatomy and Physiology 2e. OpenStax.",
     "access": "Access for free at https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/1-introduction"
    }
   },
   {
    "field": "function",
    "value": "Adipocytes also make fat: lipogenesis, which builds lipids from acetyl CoA, takes place in their cytoplasm.",
    "quote": "This process, called lipogenesis, creates lipids (fat) from the acetyl CoA and takes place in the cytoplasm of adipocytes (fat cells) and hepatocytes (liver cells).",
    "source": {
     "section": "24.3 Lipid Metabolism",
     "url": "https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/24-3-lipid-metabolism",
